    <!-- Theory: Connection Pool -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-alt)">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-center justify-between gap-3 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-(--fg-dim) hover:text-(--fg) [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <span class="font-semibold">Connection Pool — why and how</span>
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="border-t border-(--border) p-4 space-y-3 font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="space-y-2 text-[11px] text-(--fg-dim)">
            <p>Opening a DB connection is <strong class="text-(--fg)">expensive</strong>: TCP 3-way handshake → TLS negotiation → PostgreSQL auth → server allocates backend process (~5 MB). Total: <strong class="text-rose-400">10–50 ms per connection</strong>.</p>
            <p>A pool keeps <code class="text-cyan-400">N</code> connections open permanently. App threads <em>borrow</em> a slot, run their query, and return it. No new TCP connection per request.</p>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-cyan-500/25 bg-cyan-950/10 p-2.5">
              <p class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-semibold text-cyan-400">Pool sizing formula (HikariCP)</p>
              <pre class="text-[10px] text-cyan-300">{`pool_size = (core_count × 2) + disk_spindles

4 cores, SSD (1 spindle):  (4 × 2) + 1 = 9
8 cores, SSD:              (8 × 2) + 1 = 17
4 cores, 4 HDD spindles:   (4 × 2) + 4 = 12`}</pre>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-[10px] text-(--fg-faint)">Counter-intuitive: bigger pool ≠ faster. PostgreSQL processes compete for CPU and lock tables. Beyond the formula you get context-switch overhead.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-[11px] text-(--fg-dim)">
            <p><strong class="text-(--fg)">What happens when pool is full:</strong></p>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--border) bg-(--bg) p-2.5 space-y-1 text-[10px]">
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-amber-400">1.</span><span>New request waits in queue up to <code>connectionTimeout</code> (3 s default)</span></div>
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-400">2.</span><span>Timeout → <code>SQLTimeoutException</code> thrown to caller</span></div>
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-(--fg-faint)">→</span><span>This is <strong class="text-rose-400">pool exhaustion</strong> — symptom of too many slow queries or pool too small</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--border) bg-(--bg) p-2.5">
              <p class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-semibold text-(--fg-faint)">PgBouncer pooling modes</p>
              <div class="space-y-0.5 text-[10px]">
                <div><span class="text-cyan-400 w-28 inline-block">Session</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">1 conn per client session (safest)</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-amber-400 w-28 inline-block">Transaction</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">1 conn per txn (most efficient — recommended)</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-rose-400 w-28 inline-block">Statement</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">1 conn per statement (breaks txns — avoid)</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- Theory: Token Bucket -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-alt)">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-center justify-between gap-3 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-(--fg-dim) hover:text-(--fg) [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <span class="font-semibold">Token Bucket — rate limiting algorithm</span>
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="border-t border-(--border) p-4 space-y-3 font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="space-y-2 text-[11px] text-(--fg-dim)">
            <p>The token bucket is the dominant rate-limiting algorithm. It allows <strong class="text-(--fg)">bursting</strong> up to capacity while enforcing a <strong class="text-(--fg)">sustained average</strong> equal to the fill rate.</p>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-950/10 p-2.5">
              <p class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-semibold text-amber-400">Algorithm</p>
              <pre class="text-[10px] text-amber-300">{`state = { tokens: capacity, last_refill: now() }

on each request:
  elapsed = now() - state.last_refill
  state.tokens = min(capacity,
    state.tokens + elapsed × fill_rate)
  state.last_refill = now()
  if state.tokens >= 1:
    state.tokens -= 1
    return ALLOW
  else:
    return DENY (HTTP 429)`}</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-[11px] text-(--fg-dim)">
            <p><strong class="text-(--fg)">Why this works:</strong></p>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--border) bg-(--bg) p-2.5 space-y-1.5 text-[10px]">
              <div><span class="text-emerald-400">Burst:</span> <span>capacity=20 → first 20 requests pass instantly even if fill_rate=5/s</span></div>
              <div><span class="text-amber-400">Sustained:</span> <span>after burst, only 5 req/s allowed — excess dropped</span></div>
              <div><span class="text-rose-400">Penalty-free idle:</span> <span>bucket refills during quiet periods — burst credit accumulates</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--border) bg-(--bg) p-2.5">
              <p class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-semibold text-(--fg-faint)">Comparison: alternatives</p>
              <div class="space-y-0.5 text-[10px]">
                <div><span class="text-(--fg) w-28 inline-block">Fixed Window</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">simple but boundary-burst problem</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-(--fg) w-28 inline-block">Sliding Window</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">accurate, expensive (log per request)</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-amber-400 w-28 inline-block">Token Bucket</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">O(1) state, allows burst — industry standard</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-(--fg) w-28 inline-block">Leaky Bucket</span><span class="text-(--fg-dim)">constant output rate, no burst absorption</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <InfraTools />

    <!-- Pool + Token bucket explanation -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-alt)">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-center justify-between gap-3 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-(--fg-dim) hover:text-(--fg) [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <span class="font-semibold">Connection pool &amp; token bucket — how they work</span>
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="border-t border-(--border) p-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
