            <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-emerald-400">When to partition</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-[11px] list-none">
              <li>✓ Table &gt; 100 GB — planner stats degrade</li>
              <li>✓ Rolling deletes (drop old partitions in O(1))</li>
              <li>✓ Every query filters on the partition key</li>
              <li>✓ VACUUM can't keep up — partition = smaller table</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-rose-400 mt-2">When NOT to partition</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-[11px] list-none">
              <li>✗ Table &lt; 10 GB — overhead, no benefit</li>
              <li>✗ Queries rarely filter on partition key</li>
              <li>✗ Foreign keys to partitioned table (limited)</li>
              <li>✗ You need UPDATE to move a row between partitions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-(--fg-faint)">Check pruning is working</p>
            <pre class="sql-details-pre thin-scrollbar text-[10px]">{`-- Should show only matching child tables
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
SELECT * FROM orders
WHERE created_at = '2024-06-15';

-- If you see ALL partitions → pruning disabled
-- Check: partition key must be in WHERE exactly
-- enable_partition_pruning = on  (default)`}</pre>
            <pre class="sql-details-pre thin-scrollbar mt-2 text-[10px]">{`-- Partition sizes
SELECT
  child.relname AS partition,
  pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size(child.oid)) AS size
FROM pg_inherits
JOIN pg_class parent ON pg_inherits.inhparent = parent.oid
JOIN pg_class child  ON pg_inherits.inhrelid  = child.oid
WHERE parent.relname = 'orders'
ORDER BY pg_relation_size(child.oid) DESC;`}</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
